From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mhavant <matthew.hoelting@avant.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 22:36:07 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] fix(web): show the error instead of a blank page when
 rendering crashes

Any render error other than a failed chunk load unmounted the whole React
tree, leaving a blank window with nothing in the server logs. Wrap the app
in a last-resort boundary that shows the error, the component stack and
the path, with Reload and Copy details buttons.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: mhavant <matthew.hoelting@avant.com>
Signed-off-by: Desidero <desidero@gmail.com>
Docs: none (error screen shown only when the web app crashes while rendering; no setting)
